The Mercedes-Benz C32 AMG was produced from 2002 to 2004 (W203 generation). This evaluation is based on the W203 C32 AMG relative to the current automotive market.

*   **price\_usd**: As a used car from the early 2000s, the price is significantly lower than a new car today. Used prices average around $12,651 (Source [8]), with a range from $2,204 to $24,750 (Source [8]). This is well below the $35,000 average for a new car. Score: 0.80.
*   **total\_cost\_estimate\_5yr\_usd**: While the purchase price is low, an older performance luxury car will have significantly higher maintenance and potential repair costs than a new economy car (Source [16, 36]). Score: -0.80.
*   **insurance\_usd\_yr**: High-performance AMG models typically have high insurance costs due to power, value, and repair expense. The C32 was in higher insurance groups for its time (Source [22, 30, 39]). Score: -0.80.
*   **maint\_usd\_yr**: Maintenance costs for AMG models are generally very high due to specialized components and labor (Source [16, 18, 36, 40]). RepairPal estimates an annual maintenance cost of $727 for a C230 (Source [18]), the C32 AMG would be significantly higher. Score: -0.90.
*   **repair\_risk\_score**: The W203 generation is generally considered reasonably reliable for a Mercedes of its era, but the M112 V6 Kompressor engine in the C32 had known issues with the supercharger clutch/bearing and potential oil leaks (Source [2, 19, 20]). Other potential issues include steering lock failure and suspension wear (Source [2, 16, 19, 20, 21]). Risk is higher than a top-tier reliable brand and higher than standard C-Class models. Score: -0.60.
*   **hp**: 349-354 hp (Source [2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 9, 10, 13, 15, 16, 17, 18, 20, 21, 22, 23, 25]). This is significantly above the average car today. Score: 0.70.
*   **torque**: 332 lb-ft (450 Nm) (Source [2, 3, 4, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 13, 15, 17, 18, 20, 21, 23, 25]). Also well above average. Score: 0.70.
*   **cylinder\_count**: V6 (6 cylinders) (Source [2, 4, 5, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 13, 15, 17, 18, 20, 21, 23, 25]). Above the common 4 cylinders, but common for performance models of its era. Score: 0.00.
*   **engine\_displacement**: 3.2L (3199 cc) (Source [2, 4, 7, 9, 10, 11, 13, 15, 17, 18, 20, 21, 23, 25]). Around the average for a V6, but large for a modern 4-cylinder. Score: 0.00.
*   **accel\_0\_60\_sec**: Around 4.6-5.2 seconds (Source [3, 4, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 13, 16, 18, 20, 22, 29]). Very fast acceleration, comparable to many modern performance cars. Score: 0.90.
*   **top\_speed**: Electronically limited to 155 mph (250 km/h) (Source [2, 4, 7, 8, 9, 13, 15, 17, 20, 21, 27]). High top speed. Score: 0.00.
